From b3082f47dade9f9c35dde956c66b10ed5a56d02c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yusheng Peng <jiusi0519@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 19:56:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/11] fix(udp): sticky inter-device route and CIDR peer
 allowlist

A multi-homed remote announces from every interface, and
remote_[guid].peer was overwritten by the latest announce, flapping the
route between networks (e.g. WiFi/Ethernet) at the announce cadence and
hairpinning bulk traffic onto the wrong link (GW-04 freeze root cause).

- keep the established route while that peer is still present;
  handle_peer_down clears it and the next announce picks a fresh one
- new ParticipantConfig::udp_peer_allow_cidrs (TransportConfig
  likewise): presence is broadcast only on allowed interfaces and
  datagrams from other subnets are dropped; loopback is always allowed
- fail start() loudly on a malformed CIDR entry
- tests: malformed CIDR rejected, allowlist keeps loopback traffic
