From ff37dad9bae7ed751227968ec92c96156be31fb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peng Yusheng <jiusi0519@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 17:18:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 02/11] feat(mdds): harden DSoftBus Socket Bytes transport

Add generation-fenced DSoftBus callback dispatch, fd ownership fencing, deterministic Socket/Bytes tests, and explicit transport selection.

Harden ANNOUNCE QoS admission, reliable recovery, fragmentation, reordering and send-lane resource bounds; add raw ingress and lifecycle regression coverage.

Keep the tracked OpenHarmony probe artifact synchronized with its source and document the architecture.

Known follow-up: QoS-only newer ANNOUNCE snapshots still need P2 match recomputation coverage and the public matched-count comment still needs correction.
