 and QoS (reliability/history) at its own layer, transparent to DSoftBus.
 
-## Features (wire v3)
+## Features (wire v5)
 
 - Custom wire format with per-fragment flags and TLV extensions
-- Precise NACK repair and GAP-based healing for `BEST_EFFORT`/`RELIABLE`
+- Precise NACK repair and reader-addressed GAP healing for
+  `BEST_EFFORT`/`RELIABLE`; the GAP flags byte distinguishes PRE-JOIN
+  (silent advance) from EVICTED (counted lost)
+- Ordered delivery for reliable pairs (bounded per-writer reorder buffer
+  plus a participant-global budget, reserved atomically)
+- Causal join entitlement: the boundary is the writer-side association
+  sequence number — immune to cross-device clock skew and ANNOUNCE
+  one-way delay by construction (no wall-clock comparison anywhere)
+- Payload admission filters (`Reader::set_sample_filter`): rejected samples
+  never occupy queue depth or reorder budget but still advance the
+  sequence baseline (service response routing builds on this)
+- Bounded inbound memory: per-sample, per-peer and participant-global
+  reassembly caps enforced before allocation
 - Per-writer send lanes and `KEEP_ALL` backpressure
 - QoS presets with entry-point validation
 - `max_payload` probing per DSoftBus channel (falls back to a conservative
   default)
+- DSoftBus callback lifecycle hardening: generation-fenced registry with
+  in-callback drain, and an fd-reuse probe fence for late OnShutdown
+  callbacks
 
 ## Transports
 
